===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|s}}

# {{given name|male|from=Welsh}}.
#* '''1942''', {{w|Agatha Christie}}, ''Five Little Pigs'' (HarperCollins 1994, ISBN 0006163726), page 26:
#*: What was his name now? Literary sort of name - I've got it. '''Meredith'''. '''Meredith''' Blake. Don't know whether he's alive or not.
# {{surname|[[Welsh]] [[patronymic]]|from=Welsh}}
# {{given name|female|from=Welsh}}; sometimes mistaken for a combination of [[Mary]] and [[Edith]].
#* '''2004''', Jo Goodman, ''Forever In My Heart'' (Zebra Books 2004, ISBN 082177784X), page 412:
#*: "What did I hear you say her name was?"
#*: "'''Meredith'''. Mary and Edith. Names from both sides of the family."
#*: "'''Meredith'''," he repeated softly. "I like it."

Roger thought he was Meredith and violated social norms in the process.  Since when do Merediths have red hair?  I thought they were blonde.  What would Meredith do?

